# Line-ending discipline: the snapshot CSV's SHA256 is recorded over LF
# bytes; no platform may rewrite it. Keep all text LF for reproducibility.
* text=auto eol=lf
data/market_snapshot_v1.csv -text
data/SHA256SUMS.txt -text
*.pdf binary
*.png binary

# Raw generation logs and the model-written code are stored byte-for-byte.
# The manuscript states that replays are byte-identical and that the exact
# request body of every call is archived; these files were recorded with CRLF
# on Windows, so normalising their line endings on commit would make the
# published bytes differ from the bytes actually recorded. Never convert them.
runs/raw/** -text
coding/** -text
